e to them.\nL154: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? cite42†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org .\nL155: \nL156: cite43†Which authors of this paper are endorsers? | Disable MathJax (cite44†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org )\nL157: \nL158: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite45†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL159: cite46†About†info.arxiv.org · cite47†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite48†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite49†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite50†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite51†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite52†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite53†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L160: \nL161: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2511.17131v1] UI-CUBE: Enterprise-Grade Computer Use Agent Benchmarking Beyond Task Accuracy to Operational Reliability (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.17131v1)\nciteturn1947view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.17131v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 164\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Software Engineering\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 21 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:UI-CUBE: Enterprise-Grade Computer Use Agent Benchmarking Beyond Task Accuracy to Operational Reliability\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Horia Cristescu , cite6†Charles Park , cite7†Trong Canh Nguyen , cite8†Sergiu Talmacel , cite9†Alexandru-Gabriel Ilie , cite10†Stefan Adam L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled UI-CUBE: Enterprise-Grade Computer Use Agent Benchmarking Beyond Task Accuracy to Operational Reliability, by Horia Cristescu and 5 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite11†View PDF cite12†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:While current Computer Use Agent (CUA) benchmarks measure task completion effectively, they provide limited assessment of enterprise deployment readiness, emphasizing functional correctness over the operational reliability required for production systems. We present UI-CUBE (UiPath Computer Use BEnchmark), a systematic benchmark comprising 226 tasks across two difficulty tiers designed to expose fundamental architectural limitations in current CUAs.\nL17: Our evaluation covers simple UI interactions (136 tasks) and complex workflows including copy-paste tasks (50 tasks) and enterprise application scenarios (40 tasks), with systematic interface variation coverage, multi-resolution testing and automated validation of task success through the application state. Evaluation of five state-of-the-art models reveals a sharp capability cliff rather than gradual performance degradation.\nL18: Simple UI interactions achieve 67-85% success rates (compared to 97.9% human performance), but complex workflows drop precipitously to 9-19%. Human evaluators with no prior application experience achieve only 61.2% on complex tasks despite near-perfect performance on simple tasks, establishing realistic performance ceilings.\nL19: This discontinuous performance pattern -- where agents achieve 68-87% of human performance on simple tasks but only 15-32% on complex workflows -- indicates fundamental architectural limitations in memory management, hierarchical planning, and state coordination rather than incremental capability gaps addressable through better training or prompting.\nL20: UI-CUBE functions as an enterprise-readiness diagnostic, revealing that while current CUAs can manipulate individual interface elements, they cannot yet function as reliable workflow automation tools. These findings provide architectural insights essential for developing production-ready CUAs capable of managing complex, multi-step enterprise processes.\nL21: Comments:  | 18 pages, 8 figures, 5 tables. Benchmark comprising 226 tasks across two difficulty tiers. Code and benchmark available at cite13†this https URL†github.com L22: Subjects:  | Software Engineering (cs.SE); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL23: ACM (Association of Computing Machinery Classification) classes:  | I.2.0; H.5.2\nL24: Cite as:  | cite14†arXiv:2511.17131 [cs.SE]\nL25:    | (or cite15†arXiv:2511.17131v1 [cs.SE] for this version)\nL26:    | cite16†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.17131†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL27: ## Submission history\nL28: \nL29: From: Horia Cristescu [cite17†view email ]\nL30: [v1] Fri, 21 Nov 2025 10:47:22 UTC (3,813 KB)\nL31: \nL32: Full-text links:\nL33: \nL34: ## Access Paper:\nL35: \nL36: View a PDF of the paper titled UI-CUBE: Enterprise-Grade Computer Use Agent Benchmarking Beyond Task Accuracy to Operational Reliability, by Horia Cristescu and 5 other authors\nL37: \nL38:   * cite11†View PDF L39:   * cite12†HTML (experimental) L40:   * cite18†TeX Source L41: \nL42: cite19†view license†creativecommons.org L43: ### Current browse context:\nL44: \nL45: cs.SE\nL46: \nL47: cite20†< prev |   cite21†next > L48: \nL49: cite22†new | cite23†recent | cite24†2025-11 L50: \nL51: Change to browse by:\nL52: \nL53: cite25†cs L54: cite26†cs.AI L55: \nL56: ### References & Citations\nL57: \nL58:   * cite27†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L59:   * cite28†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L60:   * cite29†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L61: \nL62: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL63: \nL64: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL65: \nL66: [Button: ×]\nL67: \nL68: loading...\nL69: \nL70: Data provided by:\nL71: \nL72: ### Bookmark\nL73: \nL74: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL75: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL76: \nL77: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL78: \nL79: Bibliographic Explorer